{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivationsBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivationsBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FiniteDimensional.Defs"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.octDer_finrank_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.octDer_finrank_ge","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionDerivationsBound.lean#L77-L101","doc":"**Lower bound (fully proved):** `14 ≤ dim Der(𝕆)`.\n\n`projDer` is a left inverse of the injective linear-combination map `c ↦ Σ cᵢ · octDer i`\n(`projDer_octDer` sends the derivations to the standard basis), so `ℚ¹⁴` embeds in `Der𝕆`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.octDer_linearIndependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.octDer_linearIndependent","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionDerivationsBound.lean#L68-L75","doc":"The 14 octonion derivations are linearly independent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.projDer_octDer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.projDer_octDer","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionDerivationsBound.lean#L57-L66","doc":"The 14 derivations are sent by `projDer` to the standard basis of `ℚ¹⁴`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.projDer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.projDer","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionDerivationsBound.lean#L54-L55","doc":"`proj𝕆` restricted to the derivation space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.proj𝕆_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.proj𝕆_apply","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionDerivationsBound.lean#L51-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.proj𝕆","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.proj𝕆","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionDerivationsBound.lean#L43-L49","doc":"Projection of an endomorphism onto its 14 *free* matrix entries\n`f ↦ (t ↦ f(e_{freeB t})(freeA t))`. The 14 derivations map to the standard basis of `ℚ¹⁴`;\non `Der𝕆` it is injective (a derivation is determined by these 14 numbers). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.freeB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.freeB","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionDerivationsBound.lean#L40-L41","doc":"Column indices of the 14 free matrix-entries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.freeA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.freeA","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionDerivationsBound.lean#L36-L38","doc":"Row indices of the 14 free matrix-entries (the kernel-pivot coordinates from Gaussian\nelimination of the Leibniz-defect matrix). ","signatureChunk":0}]}